      "diveDeep": "The Twenty-One Demands were a set of coercive ultimatums sent by Japan to China in 1915 that would have greatly expanded Japanese control, provoking fierce domestic opposition. Wrong choices are incorrect because the passage focuses on national sovereignty and anti-imperialism rather than gender in industrial workplaces, corporate leadership, or Confucian values. Regents exams frequently test the geopolitical consequences of the Treaty of Versailles in East Asia, showing how the betrayal of China sparked the May Fourth Movement. The key takeaway is that imperialist aggression can act as a catalyst for political awakening and mobilization among a colonized population."
